{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Declaring-a-macro","title":"Declaring a macro","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro"},{"text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s library declares the macro and the same kind for reading. It re-exports LinkerSets,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because the expansion names LinkerSets’ types in its users’ files:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    public static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its users then register and find routes:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes the same record "},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes, in the same section, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute ("},{"code":"'@Route' applies to static members only","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it."}]},{"anchor":"Registering-types","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Registering types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record then holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":", read with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"},{"type":"text","text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/kindArgument(of:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attribute’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind:"},{"type":"text","text":" argument: an integer literal from 1 through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32.max"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kindArgument"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V","text":"AttributeSyntax"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","text":"UInt32"}],"title":"kindArgument(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/kindargument(of:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/kind(of:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kind of the record that "},{"code":"attribute","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares, from 1 through "},{"code":"UInt32.max","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/kind(of:)","required":true,"role":"symbol","title":"kind(of:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AttributeSyntax","preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/requiredConformance(of:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The protocol a type that ","type":"text"},{"code":"attribute","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" registers must conform to, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for none.","type":"text"}],"required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requiredConformance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V","text":"AttributeSyntax","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax04TypeB0V","text":"TypeSyntax","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"requiredConformance(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/requiredconformance(of:)","defaultImplementations":1,"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that turns the declaration it’s attached to into a linker-set record of one kind."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetMacro"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetMacro"}],"title":"LinkerSetMacro","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport","role":"collection","title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}}}